        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6343cec3-e48a-5797-be6f-411d116ea2d2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Jenkins Commission, Independent Commission on the Voting System\n- People: Roy Jenkins\n- Systems: Alternative Vote Plus, mixed-member electoral systems, mixed-member proportional representation, Additional Member System, majority bonus system\n- Places: United Kingdom\n- Topics: electoral reform, voting systems\n\nFacts:\n- Roy Harris Jenkins, Baron Jenkins of Hillhead, was born on 11 November 1920 and died on 5 January 2003.\n- Roy Jenkins was a British politician associated with the Labour Party, SDP, and Liberal Democrat parties, and he was also a biographer of British political leaders.\n- The Independent Commission on the Voting System was popularly known as the Jenkins Commission after its chairman Roy Jenkins.\n- The Jenkins Commission was a commission that examined possible reform of the United Kingdom electoral system.\n- In 1998, the Jenkins Commission devised Alternative Vote Plus and first proposed it as a system for elections to the Parliament of the United Kingdom.\n- Alternative Vote Plus is one of the most common mixed electoral systems.\n- Mixed-member proportional representation, Additional Member System, and the majority bonus system are also among the most common mixed electoral systems.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
